::kind(writ)

=[ Writ: tomet-syntax-lowering ]

Rules this crate must obey.

Scope is this directory. Rules that bind more than this crate live in a
`.writ.tmt` further up; read every `.writ.tmt` from here to the workspace
root, the way `.gitignore` is read.

Only the author edits this file. An agent that finds a rule in its way
proposes an edit here and stops. It does not work around the rule, and it
does not relax the rule to fit the change it wanted to make.

==[ parser-purity ]

@rule(parser-purity){
  guard: { twrit: pure }

  pure: {
    crates: [ "crates/tomet-syntax-lowering" ]
    forbid: [ "std::fs", "std::net", "std::process", "std::env" ]
    allow-external: [
      "rowan", "countme", "hashbrown", "rustc-hash", "text-size",
      "serde", "serde_core", "serde_derive",
      "proc-macro2", "quote", "syn", "unicode-ident", "unicode-width",
      "ahash", "cfg-if", "once_cell", "zerocopy", "zerocopy-derive"
    ]
  }
}

The lowering engine is pure, deterministic and side-effect-free. It performs no
I/O, resolves no external file, and executes nothing. The same input text
produces the same AST, in predictable time.
